Interview question:   Encryption and Encoding Difference
1. Encryption 🔒

Encryption is used to keep data secret.

It converts readable data (plaintext) into unreadable data (ciphertext).
Only someone with the correct key can convert it back and read it.
Main purpose: Security and Privacy

Example:

Original: Hello
Encrypted: x7#@P9!

Without the key, nobody can understand the message.

Real-life example:

WhatsApp messages
Online banking
HTTPS websites
2. Encoding 📝

Encoding is used to change the format of data so that computers can store or transmit it properly.

It is not meant for security.
Anyone who knows the encoding method can decode it.
Main purpose: Data compatibility and communication

Example (Base64 Encoding):

Original: Hello
Encoded: SGVsbG8=

Anyone can easily decode it back to "Hello".

Real-life example:

Email attachments
Web pages (UTF-8)
Base64 encoded images 

